    "preview_note": "AMAT reports fiscal Q3 (ended July 26) against a steep setup: management guided $8.95bn +/- $500m and $3.36 +/- $0.20 non-GAAP EPS after raising calendar-2026 semiconductor equipment growth to >30%. Q2 already printed a record $7.91bn and $2.86, with Semiconductor Systems at $5.97bn (DRAM 29%) and AGS +17% to $1.67bn. Three things decide the print and the tape. First, shipment conversion \u2014 they spent H1 stocking ($1.28bn capex, inventories $6.3bn, AR $6.4bn) and told investors the build plan is up; a clean $9.0bn-plus print would confirm the AI/GAA/HBM ramp is in volume, while anything near $8.5bn would reopen the Q4-FY25 China-digestion scare (China was still 27% of Q2). Second, mix and margin \u2014 GAAP GM hit 49.9% in Q2; holding 50% on a 13% sequential revenue jump is the operating tell. Third, cash conversion \u2014 Q2 FCF collapsed to $210m on working-capital absorption; a rebound above $1.2bn is required to fund the $0.53 dividend, residual buybacks and EPIC/capacity spend without stressing the $6.4bn cash pile. Q4 guide is the second-order reaction: a $9.2bn-area midpoint would validate the multi-year AI equipment thesis; a flattish or down sequential guide would imply the 30% calendar claim is front-loaded and fading.",
